Tyche — https://github.com/ayyitskevin/tyche
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Chronos's operator terminal (`chronos.terminal`, added in ADR-0018) adapts
Tyche's command-terminal design: the tolerant command grammar in which the last
registry-resolving token wins, a validated command registry serving as the single
source of truth for the panel surface and its help text, and capability gating in
which an unavailable data source renders a named, honest empty state rather than
an error or a blank.

The Chronos implementation is an independent rewrite in Python — the registry and
every panel read-model are server-side, which Tyche's design is not — but the
grammar and registry-as-truth ideas are Tyche's and are acknowledged here as the
Apache-2.0 license asks.

A copy of the Apache License, Version 2.0 is available at
http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Midas — https://github.com/ayyitskevin/midas
Licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 only.

**No Midas code is used in Chronos.** Midas was read as a design reference only,
and the influence is limited to unprotectable ideas and facts: the operator
command vocabulary (positions, orders, fills, balances, system status, alerts),
the notion of an always-visible supervision status bar, the "data honesty"
doctrine of labeling every displayed value live, stale, or unavailable, and the
conventional dark-terminal color values. This is deliberate — Chronos is
MIT-licensed and copying AGPL-licensed code into it would be incompatible.

This acknowledgement is a courtesy to the author, not an admission that any
AGPL-covered work is included, because none is.
